1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,867
A large ship enters the harbor.

2
00:00:01,867 --> 00:00:02,600
Today

3
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:06,233
is the day Beelu's cousin returns home by ship.

4
00:00:06,233 --> 00:00:08,400
Beelu and his aunt

5
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:10,033
come to the harbor to welcome him.

6
00:00:10,033 --> 00:00:11,500
Wow!

7
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:13,200
Cousin's back!

8
00:00:13,200 --> 00:00:15,833
Beelu really looks up to his cousin.

9
00:00:15,833 --> 00:00:17,533
His cousin is a sailor.

10
00:00:17,533 --> 00:00:20,867
He often tells Beelu stories about the sea.

11
00:00:20,867 --> 00:00:23,667
The story about the giant waves he encountered last time

12
00:00:23,667 --> 00:00:25,300
was thrilling and exciting.

13
00:00:25,300 --> 00:00:27,200
Beelu listened, fascinated.

14
00:00:27,867 --> 00:00:31,433
He thinks his cousin is a hero who has adventures at sea.

15
00:00:32,033 --> 00:00:33,133
I'm back!

16
00:00:34,900 --> 00:00:35,967
Hey, kid!

17
00:00:36,600 --> 00:00:39,200
I brought you a present!

18
00:00:39,200 --> 00:00:40,467
Wow!

19
00:00:42,067 --> 00:00:43,733
Looks a little too big.

20
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:45,967
No way!

21
00:00:45,967 --> 00:00:47,667
I'll grow into it in no time!

22
00:00:47,667 --> 00:00:49,733
Then I'll be just like you, Cousin,

23
00:00:49,733 --> 00:00:51,433
having adventures at sea!

24
00:00:51,433 --> 00:00:53,033
Hahaha!

25
00:00:53,033 --> 00:00:55,667
Working on a ship isn't an adventure, you know.

26
00:00:55,667 --> 00:00:56,600
Suddenly,

27
00:00:56,600 --> 00:00:58,467
a sea breeze blows by

28
00:00:58,467 --> 00:01:01,167
and sends the sailor's hat flying into the air.

29
00:01:01,167 --> 00:01:01,933
Ah!

30
00:01:01,933 --> 00:01:04,500
Beelu reaches out to catch it,

31
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:05,933
but misses.

32
00:01:05,933 --> 00:01:08,500
The hat blows into the container yard.

33
00:01:08,500 --> 00:01:09,767
I'll go get it!

34
00:01:10,833 --> 00:01:11,533
Beelu!

35
00:01:11,533 --> 00:01:12,433
Wait!

36
00:01:13,267 --> 00:01:15,167
Everyone is too late to stop him.

37
00:01:16,167 --> 00:01:18,367
Following the direction the hat blew,

38
00:01:18,367 --> 00:01:21,567
Beelu reaches the container storage area.

39
00:01:21,567 --> 00:01:24,733
It's like a maze made of steel.

40
00:01:24,733 --> 00:01:25,933
Beelu thinks

41
00:01:25,933 --> 00:01:28,600
searching the maze for his new hat

42
00:01:28,600 --> 00:01:31,267
is just like an exciting adventure.

43
00:01:31,833 --> 00:01:34,633
Could this be the Adventure God's test for me?

44
00:01:35,067 --> 00:01:37,767
Beelu, who dreams of becoming an adventurer,

45
00:01:37,767 --> 00:01:39,400
shouts excitedly.

46
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:41,800
Yay!

47
00:01:42,400 --> 00:01:43,300
Wow!

48
00:01:43,300 --> 00:01:46,067
Kid, don't come over here!

49
00:01:46,067 --> 00:01:48,567
A giraffe shouts from around the corner.

50
00:01:48,567 --> 00:01:50,833
Beelu almost bumps into her.

51
00:01:51,900 --> 00:01:53,000
Sorry!

52
00:01:54,067 --> 00:01:55,833
It's okay, it's okay.

53
00:01:55,833 --> 00:01:57,700
Watch where you're going!

54
00:01:58,367 --> 00:02:01,233
The giraffe looks very flustered.

55
00:02:01,233 --> 00:02:03,633
But Beelu is focused on finding his hat

56
00:02:03,633 --> 00:02:05,433
and leaves without thinking much of it.

57
00:02:06,400 --> 00:02:07,400
Phew...

58
00:02:07,400 --> 00:02:08,600
That was close.

59
00:02:10,400 --> 00:02:12,267
Beelu keeps walking

60
00:02:12,267 --> 00:02:13,500
until he reaches a dead end.

61
00:02:13,500 --> 00:02:15,033
He still can't find his hat.

62
00:02:15,733 --> 00:02:17,167
That's strange.

63
00:02:17,167 --> 00:02:18,700
I looked really carefully.

64
00:02:20,333 --> 00:02:22,433
How could it be missing?

65
00:02:23,133 --> 00:02:24,567
On his way back,

66
00:02:24,567 --> 00:02:27,267
Beelu runs into the giraffe again.

67
00:02:27,667 --> 00:02:28,700
But this time,

68
00:02:28,700 --> 00:02:31,000
the giraffe is floating in midair!

69
00:02:35,967 --> 00:02:38,233
When the giraffe sees Beelu,

70
00:02:38,233 --> 00:02:39,467
she smiles awkwardly.

71
00:02:40,367 --> 00:02:41,933
The two stare at each other.

72
00:02:41,933 --> 00:02:44,600
Uh...

73
00:02:44,600 --> 00:02:46,300
Could you be...?

74
00:02:46,300 --> 00:02:48,900
That's right, I am

75
00:02:48,900 --> 00:02:51,000
a wizard!

76
00:02:52,767 --> 00:02:53,733
Hello.

77
00:02:53,733 --> 00:02:55,400
My name is Qi Lin.

78
00:02:55,400 --> 00:02:56,733
I'm Beelu!

79
00:02:57,867 --> 00:02:59,600
Ahhh! Beelu!

80
00:02:59,600 --> 00:03:02,000
You mustn't tell anyone!

81
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:03,467
No problem.

82
00:03:03,467 --> 00:03:05,167
But, Sister Qi Lin,

83
00:03:05,167 --> 00:03:07,167
what are you doing here?

84
00:03:07,167 --> 00:03:08,433
Are you a sailor, too?

85
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:10,233
Actually,

86
00:03:10,233 --> 00:03:13,300
I've come to pick up a magic letter from my mentor.

87
00:03:13,300 --> 00:03:14,100
Oh?

88
00:03:14,100 --> 00:03:15,600
At the harbor?

89
00:03:15,600 --> 00:03:17,267
Beelu imagines

90
00:03:17,267 --> 00:03:21,033
that wizards would appear somewhere more mysterious.

91
00:03:21,033 --> 00:03:23,067
When wizards around the world

92
00:03:23,067 --> 00:03:24,667
need to communicate in secret,

93
00:03:24,667 --> 00:03:27,434
they hide messages inside objects.

94
00:03:27,434 --> 00:03:30,100
Shipping containers are perfect for that!

95
00:03:30,100 --> 00:03:31,100
They're huge

96
00:03:31,100 --> 00:03:33,266
and can store lots of messages.

97
00:03:33,266 --> 00:03:35,900
They travel all over the world,

98
00:03:35,900 --> 00:03:38,834
so we write messages inside containers

99
00:03:38,834 --> 00:03:41,434
and let other wizards know where to collect them.

100
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:44,900
Wow!

101
00:03:44,900 --> 00:03:46,100
That's so cool!

102
00:03:46,100 --> 00:03:49,000
You have to search through all these containers?

103
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:50,700
That must be really hard!

104
00:03:50,700 --> 00:03:53,733
There are countless containers here.

105
00:03:53,733 --> 00:03:54,500
No,

106
00:03:54,500 --> 00:03:55,867
I've already found it.

107
00:03:55,867 --> 00:03:57,300
It's right behind me.

108
00:03:57,300 --> 00:04:00,833
But I need to stand on a magic circle,

109
00:04:00,833 --> 00:04:04,667
and that circle is on top of the container.

110
00:04:04,667 --> 00:04:06,567
Whether I climb

111
00:04:06,567 --> 00:04:08,633
or use a levitation spell,

112
00:04:08,633 --> 00:04:10,467
I can't reach the top.

113
00:04:13,233 --> 00:04:15,967
Qi Lin isn't very good at levitation spells.

114
00:04:15,967 --> 00:04:17,367
She can't fly very high,

115
00:04:17,367 --> 00:04:19,233
and she wobbles all over the place.

116
00:04:20,367 --> 00:04:22,333
Maybe I can help you.

117
00:04:22,333 --> 00:04:23,767
Lift me up

118
00:04:23,767 --> 00:04:25,833
and I can get to the magic circle

119
00:04:25,833 --> 00:04:27,200
to retrieve it for you!

120
00:04:28,033 --> 00:04:28,900
Huh?

121
00:04:28,900 --> 00:04:30,133
That might work!

122
00:04:30,967 --> 00:04:33,800
Then could you help me find my hat afterward?

123
00:04:34,633 --> 00:04:36,900
Of course!

124
00:04:37,700 --> 00:04:40,467
Beelu and Qi Lin make a deal.

125
00:04:41,200 --> 00:04:43,967
Qi Lin lifts Beelu up in her mouth.

126
00:04:43,967 --> 00:04:46,800
Then Beelu grabs onto the container.

127
00:04:46,800 --> 00:04:48,067
He swings his right leg over

128
00:04:48,067 --> 00:04:50,033
and successfully climbs onto the container.

129
00:04:51,167 --> 00:04:53,833
The hat is on this very container!

130
00:04:53,833 --> 00:04:56,100
Beelu thinks he's incredibly lucky!

131
00:04:57,267 --> 00:05:00,267
Just as Beelu is about to pick up the hat,

132
00:05:00,267 --> 00:05:01,667
an even stronger gust of wind

133
00:05:01,667 --> 00:05:03,333
blows it even farther away!

134
00:05:03,900 --> 00:05:07,100
The hat flies so far it's almost out of sight.

135
00:05:09,967 --> 00:05:12,300
Can you see the magic circle?

136
00:05:13,833 --> 00:05:14,900
Yes.

137
00:05:14,900 --> 00:05:16,967
Then stand on the magic circle.

138
00:05:17,667 --> 00:05:18,600
Okay.

139
00:05:18,600 --> 00:05:20,267
I'm standing on it now.

140
00:05:20,800 --> 00:05:23,364
Qi Lin recites

141
00:05:23,364 --> 00:05:25,825
a spell that Beelu can't understand.

142
00:05:25,825 --> 00:05:29,067
Beelu falls into the glowing magic circle.

143
00:05:29,900 --> 00:05:31,567
Inside the container,

144
00:05:31,567 --> 00:05:33,967
Beelu feels as if he's in a fantasy world.

145
00:05:34,833 --> 00:05:38,367
He floats weightlessly in the middle of the container.

146
00:05:38,933 --> 00:05:41,333
I'm going to search the container's history now.

147
00:05:41,333 --> 00:05:43,133
It might take a little while.

148
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:47,167
Outside a factory in Vietnam,

149
00:05:47,167 --> 00:05:49,133
bundles of brown fabric

150
00:05:49,133 --> 00:05:51,333
are carried from a shipping container into the factory.

151
00:05:52,133 --> 00:05:54,167
The fabric is made into backpacks

152
00:05:54,167 --> 00:05:55,500
and packed into boxes again,

153
00:05:55,500 --> 00:05:57,567
then shipped to the Port of Calais.

154
00:05:57,567 --> 00:05:58,300
Huh?

155
00:05:58,300 --> 00:06:00,167
Isn't that my backpack?

156
00:06:00,700 --> 00:06:03,967
It turns out Beelu's backpack came from somewhere else.

157
00:06:04,567 --> 00:06:06,467
At Kaohsiung Harbor in Taiwan,

158
00:06:06,467 --> 00:06:08,033
the backpacks are unloaded

159
00:06:08,033 --> 00:06:10,467
and bananas are loaded into the container.

160
00:06:10,467 --> 00:06:12,533
The container, now full of bananas,

161
00:06:12,533 --> 00:06:14,733
races along a highway in Japan.

162
00:06:15,433 --> 00:06:17,033
Looks like it isn't in this part.

163
00:06:17,600 --> 00:06:19,100
I'll speed up the search!

164
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:21,200
Out at sea,

165
00:06:21,200 --> 00:06:23,267
the ship encounters a storm.

166
00:06:23,267 --> 00:06:24,767
Water splashes

167
00:06:24,767 --> 00:06:26,700
against the metal container.

168
00:06:27,633 --> 00:06:31,067
Many large ships leave the harbor together.

169
00:06:31,067 --> 00:06:34,367
Beelu seems to smell the pungent scent of gasoline.

170
00:06:35,333 --> 00:06:37,333
On the Suez Canal,

171
00:06:37,333 --> 00:06:39,533
the ship slowly passes by.

172
00:06:39,533 --> 00:06:42,400
An endless desert stretches alongside it.

173
00:06:43,267 --> 00:06:47,167
Beelu travels all over the world with the container,

174
00:06:47,167 --> 00:06:49,433
as it carries all kinds of cargo.

175
00:06:49,433 --> 00:06:50,500
Wow!

176
00:06:50,500 --> 00:06:53,733
This container has been to so many places

177
00:06:53,733 --> 00:06:56,033
and carried so many things!

178
00:06:56,033 --> 00:06:57,367
I found it!

179
00:06:57,367 --> 00:06:58,467
Suddenly,

180
00:06:58,467 --> 00:07:00,967
they arrive at the Port of Bremen.

181
00:07:00,967 --> 00:07:03,933
A mysterious bird passes through the container.

182
00:07:03,933 --> 00:07:07,000
The light in its hand gathers into a letter.

183
00:07:07,833 --> 00:07:09,567
Catch, child.

184
00:07:10,367 --> 00:07:12,333
The moment Beelu catches the letter,

185
00:07:12,333 --> 00:07:13,700
he realizes

186
00:07:13,700 --> 00:07:15,800
he's back on top of the container.

187
00:07:16,367 --> 00:07:18,033
The journey is over.

188
00:07:19,400 --> 00:07:20,567
Here you go.

189
00:07:20,567 --> 00:07:21,667
Great!

190
00:07:21,667 --> 00:07:23,867
Now it's my turn to help you find your hat!

191
00:07:23,867 --> 00:07:24,867
Ah!

192
00:07:24,867 --> 00:07:26,367
But just now,

193
00:07:26,367 --> 00:07:28,600
your hat blew out of the harbor.

194
00:07:29,300 --> 00:07:30,700
I see.

195
00:07:31,433 --> 00:07:32,367
No problem.

196
00:07:32,367 --> 00:07:34,500
I'll use the magic I'm good at!

197
00:07:34,500 --> 00:07:36,300
Can you describe what your hat looks like?

198
00:07:36,833 --> 00:07:37,467
Huh?

199
00:07:38,433 --> 00:07:39,700
A little while later,

200
00:07:39,700 --> 00:07:41,333
Beelu's aunt and cousin

201
00:07:41,333 --> 00:07:43,233
finally find him.

202
00:07:44,200 --> 00:07:45,433
Good grief!

203
00:07:45,433 --> 00:07:46,700
You ran off so fast!

204
00:07:46,700 --> 00:07:47,933
Are you hurt?

205
00:07:49,333 --> 00:07:50,133
No!

206
00:07:50,133 --> 00:07:50,933
Cousin!

207
00:07:50,933 --> 00:07:53,767
I just had a huge adventure!

208
00:07:55,000 --> 00:07:55,933
Really?

209
00:07:55,933 --> 00:07:56,933
That's good.

210
00:07:56,933 --> 00:07:57,600
Yeah.

211
00:07:57,600 --> 00:07:59,067
Today was so much fun!
